# Test-Konventionen

## API-Tests (Vitest + Supertest)

Testdateien neben der Quelldatei ablegen:

```
apps/api/src/nvm/
├── nvm.parser.ts
├── nvm.parser.spec.ts   ← Unit-Test
├── nvm.service.ts
└── nvm.service.spec.ts  ← Unit-Test (mit Mocks)
apps/api/src/routes/
└── nvm.routes.spec.ts   ← Integrations-Test mit Supertest
```

Unit-Test-Muster:

```typescript
// nvm.parser.spec.ts
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { parseInstalledVersions } from './nvm.parser.js';

describe('parseInstalledVersions', () => {
  it('erkennt die aktive Version', () => {
    const stdout = '->     v22.11.0 (default)\n       v20.5.0';
    const result = parseInstalledVersions(stdout);
    expect(result).toHaveLength(2);
    expect(result[0].active).toBe(true);
    expect(result[0].default).toBe(true);
    expect(result[0].version).toBe('22.11.0');
  });

  it('gibt leeres Array bei leerem Input zurück', () => {
    expect(parseInstalledVersions('')).toEqual([]);
  });
});
```

Integrations-Test mit Supertest:

```typescript
// nvm.routes.spec.ts
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest';
import request from 'supertest';
import app from '../../server.js';
import * as nvmService from '../nvm/nvm.service.js';

vi.mock('../nvm/nvm.service.js');

describe('POST /api/versions/install', () => {
  it('lehnt ungültige Version mit 400 ab', async () => {
    const res = await request(app).post('/api/versions/install').send({ version: '../etc/passwd' });
    expect(res.status).toBe(400);
  });

  it('gibt 200 bei gültiger Version zurück', async () => {
    vi.mocked(nvmService.install).mockResolvedValue({ stdout: 'ok', stderr: '' });
    const res = await request(app).post('/api/versions/install').send({ version: '22' });
    expect(res.status).toBe(200);
  });
});
```

## Angular-Tests (Vitest + @testing-library/angular)

```typescript
// version-card.component.spec.ts
import { render, screen, fireEvent } from '@testing-library/angular';
import { VersionCardComponent } from './version-card.component';

describe('VersionCardComponent', () => {
  it('deaktiviert Buttons während isLoading', async () => {
    const { fixture } = await render(VersionCardComponent);
    const comp = fixture.componentInstance;
    comp.isLoading.set(true);
    fixture.detectChanges();
    expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /installieren/i })).toBeDisabled();
  });
});
```

## Vitest-Konfiguration (API – `vitest.config.ts`)

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config';

export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    globals: true,
    environment: 'node',
    include: ['src/**/*.spec.ts'],
    coverage: {
      provider: 'v8',
      reporter: ['text', 'lcov'],
      include: ['src/**/*.ts'],
      exclude: ['src/**/*.spec.ts'],
      thresholds: { lines: 70, functions: 70 },
    },
  },
});
```

## Playwright E2E (`apps/e2e/`)

```typescript
// install-flow.spec.ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('Kann eine Node-Version installieren', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('http://localhost:4200');
  await expect(page.getByText('nvm Manager')).toBeVisible();
  await page.getByLabel('Version').fill('22');
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Installieren' }).click();
  await expect(page.getByText(/Installiere/)).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Benennungsregeln

- Testdateien: `*.spec.ts` (Unit/Integration), `*.e2e.ts` (Playwright)
- `describe`-Blöcke: Klassenname oder Funktionsname
- `it`-Texte: auf Deutsch, verhalten beschreibend ("gibt 400 zurück wenn...")
- Mocks immer über `vi.mock()`, kein manuelles Stub-Patching
